  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study - Distributed Energy Resource Deployment, through Government of India</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USTDA is providing $459,283 to partially fund a feasibility study (FS) to develop a distributed energy resource (DER) plan for Tata Power Delhi Distribution Limited&apos;s (TPDDL) service territory in North Delhi, India. The project will develop integrated planning tools and metrics to enable TPDDL to select distributed energy resources that have the potential to improve the reliability of TPDDL&apos;s system, reduce its environmental footprint, and reduce its overall costs to customers. Special emphasis will be given to power generation from renewables and demand response technologies.</narrative>
  </description>
